+## T122. Move my data (0270)
+
+Do this on a register you can afford to experiment with, ideally with a Shopify shop that has a few items, a collection and some customers.
+
+1. Settings, Connections, scroll to **Move my data**. Choose copy from **Shopify** and copy to **Pure Tillium**, then tap **See what would be copied**. Pass: it shows counts for items and stock, collections and customers, a list of what is not copied (order history, gift cards, discounts, pictures), and nothing has changed yet.
+2. Tap **Copy to Pure Tillium**, then **Copy** on the confirmation. Pass: progress words appear, then "Done." with the counts matching step 1.
+3. Save Pure Tillium as the Catalogue connection and open the till. Pass: the items, prices and stock match Shopify, the collection holds the right items, and the customers are searchable.
+4. Open Move my data again with the same two choices. Pass: it says everything is already there and the button says Nothing to copy.
+5. Turn airplane mode on part way through a copy. Pass: it stops with a plain message, and after turning it off, running it again copies only the rest.
+6. Turn on practice mode and try a copy. Pass: it refuses and copies nothing.
+7. Check Shopify. Pass: nothing in it changed.
+
+Tell me pass or fail for each, and the exact text of any error.
